<title>INDIA: India BSE cuts circuit limit on A group stocks.</title>
<headline>India BSE cuts circuit limit on A group stocks.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) has decided to reduce the circuit limits on the prices of all A group stocks effective from Tuesday, the BSE said.</p>
<p>The circuit limits -- which prevents prices moving beyond a prescribed up-or-down range -- will remain till the end of the current settlement ending on October 11, the BSE said in a notice.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
